Architecture plan for Issue #234: Point the header "Home" nav link to https://ideavibes.ai

Scope and module structure
- Shared layout/navigation code:
  - `rust-backend/src/html/layout.rs` owns the shared `LayoutTemplate` context and constructs the header navigation links used by the Askama layout.
  - `rust-backend/templates/partials/header.html` renders those `nav_links`; it should not need structural changes if the link data is updated in Rust.
- Shared layout tests:
  - `rust-backend/src/html/mod.rs` contains rendering assertions for the shared public layout/header/footer and should be updated to expect the external Home nav link.
- No shared types, database schema, API routes, auth/session logic, object storage, or Tailwind styling changes are needed.

Dependencies between issues
- This batch contains only Issue #234.
- It is independent of footer logo/link behavior, post rendering, newsletter signup, admin flows, and SEO sitemap/breadcrumb helpers.

Key design decisions
- Product brand remains Ideavibes as stated by the issue and existing templates.
- Change only the header navigation item labeled `Home` so its `href` is `https://ideavibes.ai`.
- Preserve the header logo link to the blog root `/` unless an issue explicitly requests changing it.
- Keep the existing Askama partial loop and nav styling unchanged; use the existing `NavLink` data path for the href update.
- Validate with the Rust backend tests (`npm run backend:test` or `cargo test --manifest-path rust-backend/Cargo.toml`).
